# vauth is an identity provider. The files below decide who can log in, who is
# an admin, and where authorization codes are delivered — a bad change to any of
# them is invisible in a quick review and compromises every account.
#
# These require a maintainer's review. This is not distrust of contributors; it
# is the same reason Postgres has committers. Contribute freely everywhere else.

